:{"href":"/en/tip/20-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"Use water hotter than 70 °C to prepare formula, then let it cool before feeding; discard any leftovers"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/20-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Do not feed honey to children under 1 year old"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/20-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Vitamin K injection at birth is essential"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/20-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Infants under 3 months with a body temperature of 38°C should be taken straight to the hospital — no home observation needed"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/20-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"No matter how tired or angry you are, never shake a baby"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/20-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"When choosing diapers, focus on three things: fit, how often you change them, and whether they’ve been flagged in any quality inspections"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/20-11","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Consider buying big-ticket items in the order “borrow, buy used, buy new” — don’t buy them all at once"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/20-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"For children with severe eczema or egg allergy, don’t avoid peanuts — introduce them early under medical guidance, but never feed whole peanuts"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/20-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Watch newborn jaundice for these signals: yellow within 24 hours of birth, getting yellower, hard to wake or refusing feeds, pale stools — go to hospital the same day"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/20-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children