nd-hand supply far exceeds demand. Keep…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Consider buying big-ticket items in the order “borrow, buy used, buy new” — don’t buy them all at once"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No extra money is needed; the amount saved is usually in the thousands of yuan. The hard part is resisting the urge to buy everything at once."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Strollers, cribs, baby wraps and toys have short useful lives, and second-hand supply far exceeds demand. Keep three safety boundaries. First, car seats: the US National Highway Traffic Safety Administration says to replace a seat after a moderate or severe crash and never reuse it. A crash counts as minor only if all five conditions hold: the car can be driven away, the door nearest the seat is undamaged, nobody was injured, airbags did not deploy, and the seat has no visible damage. A used seat is usable only if five things can be confirmed: no moderate or severe crash, a manufacturing-date and model label, no recall, all parts present, and the instructions available. The date and model allow checks for recalls and excessive age. Second, mattresses: a Scottish case-control study compared babies who died suddenly with healthy babies of the same age and looked back at mattress use. Routinely sleeping on another child's mattress was associated with higher sudden infant death syndrome risk (OR 3.07, about 3 times, 95% CI 1.51–6.22). For a mattress from another household it was 4.78; from the same household, 1.64, with the latter not showing a clear difference. The authors said evidence was insufficient to establish that the mattress itself caused it. Third, cribs: the US introduced mandatory new crib standards on June 28, 2011, also covering second-hand cribs. Traditional drop-side designs were eliminated. The US Consumer Product Safety Commission says compliance requires destructive testing, so it cannot provide a self-check method. From November 2007 to April 2010, 147 deaths involving full-size cribs were reported in the US: 35 involved structural problems and 18 involved drop-side failures. Loose screws caused at least 10 deaths. US law bans inclined infant sleepers regardless of production year, with the ban written into regulatory rules in 2023 (US, UK)."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["省钱部分为作者经验，无直接文献；US NHTSA. Car Seat Use After a Crash. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.nhtsa.gov/car-seats-and-booster-seats/car-seat-use-after-crash","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.nhtsa.gov/car-seats-and-booster-seats/car-seat-use-after-crash"]},"；US NHTSA. Used Car Seat Safety Checklist. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.nhtsa.gov/car-seats-and-booster-seats/used-car-seat-safety-checklist","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.nhtsa.gov/car-seats-and-booster-seats/used-car-seat-safety-checklist"]},"；Tappin D, Brooke H, Ecob R, Gibson A (2002). Used infant mattresses and sudden infant death syndrome in Scotland: case-control study. BMJ, 325(7371), 1007. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.325.7371.1007","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.325.7371.1007"]},"；Blair P, Fleming P, Smith I (1997). Case-control study of sudden infant death syndrome in Scotland. Income level or bed sharing would confound any effect of previous use of mattress. BMJ, 315(7111), 812. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.315.7111.812a","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.315.7111.812a"]},"；US Consumer Product Safety Commission (2010). Safety Standards for Full-Size Baby Cribs and Non-Full-Size Baby Cribs; Final Rule. Federal Register 2010-32178. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2010/12/28/2010-32178/safety-standards-for-full-size-baby-cribs-and-non-full-size-baby-cribs-final-rule","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2010/12/28/2010-32178/safety-standards-for-full-size-baby-cribs-and-non-full-size-baby-cribs-final-rule"]},"；US Consumer Product Safety Commission (2023). Ban of Inclined Sleepers for Infants. Federal Register 2023-17350. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/08/16/2023-17350/ban-of-inclined-sleepers-for-infants","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/08/16/2023-17350/ban-of-inclined-sleepers-for-infants"]},"；冲动消费见第 5 节"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.nhtsa.gov/car-seats-and-booster-seats/car-seat-use-after-crash","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["The evidence grade remains C because the savings side lacks literature. All three safety boundaries have sources, but from the US and UK. No specific official Chinese guidance on used cribs or car seats was found. The mattress study has been challenged: a 1997 letter argued household income and bed-sharing could confound the second-hand mattress association. For car seats, see Section 1, item 10. For infant sleep position and bedding, see item 1 of this section (sleeping on the back). The book neither endorses nor reje